ds a Lean proof of exactly this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-lower-bound-every-reset"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-lower-bound-every-reset"],"id":"long.thm-lower-bound-every-reset","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 9.46 (A: a sufficient lower bound at every reset)","locator":"Long record Theorem 9.46, p. 111, label thm:lower-bound-every-reset","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Assume that $|\\mathrm{rem}(r+1)-2^{r+1}|>2^{(r+5)/2}$ for every upper or middle reset $r\\ge10$. Then $1/2\\in\\mathcal A$.*\n\n*Here is the role of the constants. Put\n$$\nB(r)=2^{\\lfloor(r+4)/2\\rfloor}+2r+3.\n$$\nFor $r\\ge10$, one has $B(r)^2\\le2^{r+5}$. A right branch at the first crossing of the largest omitted rank $r$ would force $|\\Delta_{r+1}|\\le B(r)$, by tracing the exact affine recurrence back to that reset. The assumed strict lower bound excludes this crossing. The largest-skip induction then gives half-membership. The hypothesis concerns every actual reset beyond the threshold; neither a long finite check nor an asserted run-length asymptotic supplies it.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-lower-bound-every-reset","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-lower-bound-every-reset","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-lower-bound-every-reset%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.half_mem_mersenneAchievementSet_of_resetSqrtEscape%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-lower-bound-every-reset%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.half_mem_mersenneAchievementSet_of_resetSqrtEscape%22%2C%22fo